{"term":"discover","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d2438ef854c8a998da","definition":"To find or learn something for the first time.","example":"Turning the corner, I discovered a lovely little shop. I discovered that they sold widgets.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["come across","find"],"antonyms":["conceal","cover","cover up","hide","miss","overlook"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["detect","find","invent","stumble upon"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6ae77ea5f505b713a3","definition":"To remove the cover from; to uncover (a head, building etc.).","example":"He set down his bags beside him, on the beautiful red floor, and he took off his hat, for he had reached his destination, discovering his scant red hair, and laid it on the table beside him.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["catch","check","come upon","detect","determine","discover","disinter","fish up","identify","learn","locate","map","navigate","pick up","pinpoint","place","position","recognize","search","spot","trace","track","unearth","explore"],"antonyms":["conceal","cover","cover up","hide","miss","overlook"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["detect","find","invent","stumble upon"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:20d7ce86e7b7953b50","definition":"To expose, uncover.","example":"The gust of wind discovered a bone in the sand.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["expose","reveal","uncover"],"antonyms":["conceal","cover","cover up","hide","miss","overlook"],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["detect","find","invent","stumble upon"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d6f24eceac2cac4988","definition":"To create by moving a piece out of another piece's line of attack.","example":"This move discovers an attack on a vital pawn.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["catch","check","come upon","detect","determine","discover","disinter","fish up","identify","learn","locate","map","navigate","pick up","pinpoint","place","position","recognize","search","spot","trace","track","unearth","explore"],"antonyms":["conceal","cover","cover up","hide","miss","overlook"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["detect","find","invent","stumble upon"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3ba57407005541e494","definition":"To question (a person) as part of discovery in a lawsuit.","example":"Indeed, the plaintiffs suggest that they may not need to call Ms. Samji at all if they are allowed to discover the defendant on the new documents before any new trial takes place.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["catch","check","come upon","detect","determine","discover","disinter","fish up","identify","learn","locate","map","navigate","pick up","pinpoint","place","position","recognize","search","spot","trace","track","unearth","explore"],"antonyms":["conceal","cover","cover up","hide","miss","overlook"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["detect","find","invent","stumble upon"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:76da952169b42e5741","definition":"To reveal (information); to divulge, make known.","example":"I discovered my plans to the rest of the team.","pos":"verb","